<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίθιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, Adj., name of a
		kind of grape, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταφυλή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					5.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. Verg.<i><span class="en">
				<u>G.</u>
				2.93
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.269
			</span></i>, Stat.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Silv.</u>
				4.9.38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ ψιθίης ἑλίνοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					181
				</span></i>
			: hence was made 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίθιος οἶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					138
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), cf. Anaxandr<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				14.80
			</span></i>:—also spelt <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψύθιος</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταφυλὰ ψ.</span>”
				<i>Docum. ined. dell' Africa Italiana</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.86
				</span></i>
			, al. (Cyrene, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>), v. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> cc.</div>
